    delphi:hasConfidence "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The universal prediction is clear and searchable in a large public record. Confirming non-reappearance is asymmetric and taxonomic identity is imperfect, but counterexamples can decisively refute it." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Search dated occurrence records for species with a substantial global absence followed by later occurrences, then audit taxonomy and dating. A validated reappearance of the identical biological species would refute the claim; no such cases supports it only within detection limits." ;
